1. Any-precision encoding of the experts (ocdpa/encoder.py)
   The encoding method is that of DPA-MoE (Kim et al.): nested sign planes with shared, descending scales and an
   offset per group of 128 inputs, fitted progressively from 2 to 8 planes. The numerical kernels of the encoder
   (greedy initialisation, least-squares refinement, nearest-level assignment, conjugate gradient) are adapted from
   AnyBCQ, https://github.com/naver-aics/anybcq,
   Copyright (c) 2025-present NAVER Cloud Corp., licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   AnyBCQ in turn refers to https://github.com/allenbai01/ProxQuant.
   Changes: only the asymmetric (offset) variant without sample weights is kept, the kernels and the progressive
   expansion are gathered in one module, and unrelated code (training, packing, evaluation) is removed.
   The upstream license and notice are reproduced in licenses/AnyBCQ-LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt and
   licenses/AnyBCQ-NOTICE.txt.

